course: dictionary
lesson: 10271
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Topping» usually means food put on top of another food, but old-fashioned UK slang uses it to mean excellent. Read the words around it to decide.
explain: «Frozen pizzas get toppings from machines, sometimes falling like snow from hoppers, then are frozen fast in a cold tunnel.» The sentence is about pizza and machines, so toppings must be things put on the pizza. Ask: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Topping can also be a verb form. «Topping up» means filling something again, like topping up a phone or a drink. The spelling is the same, but the job the word does changes. Look at the words before and after it to spot which job it is doing.
fact: A topping is food put on top of another food, such as pizza toppings or an ice-cream topping.
fact: «Topping» in old-fashioned UK slang means excellent, as in «What a topping idea!»
fact: «Topping up» means filling something up again, such as a drink or a phone.
fact: «Frozen pizzas get toppings from machines, sometimes falling like snow from hoppers.» The pizzas are then frozen fast, because fast freezing makes small ice crystals that damage food less.
fact: Frozen pizzas must be cooked until they are hot all the way through.
exercise: «Frozen pizzas get toppings from machines, sometimes falling like snow from hoppers.» In this sentence, what are toppings? | *Food put on top of the pizza | The hoppers that hold the flour | Machines that make the pizza | Cold tunnels for freezing
exercise: Old school story: «What a topping idea!» What does topping mean here? | Coming down like snow | *Excellent | Heavy and wet | Hidden under a cloth
exercise: Ella says, «I'll go and top up my phone.» What does topping up mean? | *Filling it again with credit | Dropping it on the floor | Turning the phone off | Making it into a pizza
test: The sentence says fast freezing makes small ice crystals. Why is this good? | It stops the food being cooked | It makes ice crystals bigger | *It damages food less | It makes the food spicy
test: What must frozen pizza be until it is safe to eat? | Cut into small squares | Left out to thaw for a week | Eaten straight from the freezer | *Cooked until hot all the way through
exam: In «The team is topping the league this year», what does topping mean? | Covering with cheese | *Being number one, at the top | Falling like snow | Old and tired
